{"availability":"available","full":"kenlasko/k8s","name":"k8s","description":"My personal Kubernetes cluster running SideroLabs Talos OS via Omni and managed by ArgoCD","category":"Developer tools","language":"Shell","stars":5,"forks":1,"created":"2025-04-18T14:02:35Z","updated":"2026-10-09T14:40:43Z","branch":"main","homepage":"","topics":["kubesearch"],"demo":"https://monize-demo.laskonet.com/","color":"#302e55","ink":"#dbd2ff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T15:39:42.563Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-09T15:39:42.563Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-09T15:39:42.563Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-09T15:39:42.563Z","stars":5,"forks":1}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["This is the Git repository that contains all the configuration for my multiple homelab Kubernetes clusters. The clusters are used to host a number of self-hosted services mostly focused on movies and TV show management Linux ISOs along with all the supporting software. This repository is fully gitops-optimized and is managed by ArgoCD.","The clusters are built on Sidero Lab's Talos OS using on-prem Omni for low-level cluster management.","I started with Docker containers on Raspberry Pis several years ago and as my usage grew, so did my desire to make things more resilient to failures. I eventually moved away from Docker on a single RPi to K3S on two or three mini-PCs. That eventually grew into its current iteration on 7 mini-PCs using Talos. It has proven to be extremely stable and resilient to hardware failures. Day-to-day management is minimal. As long as I freeze automatic updates during extended vacations (via Renovate), the cluster functions without intervention for months at a time. As I enjoy tinkering, most issues are…"],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/kenlasko/k8s/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"ccf47b0ceeeaff3925033ec840ed4b26b3eda3a7795442c28f5c4fcecb4e973e","extractedAt":"2026-10-09T15:39:42.708Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T15:39:42.708Z",